1002. Find Common Characters
Given a string array words, return an array of all characters that show up in all strings within the words (including duplicates). 
You may return the answer in any order.

Explanation:

Intuition:We need characters that appear in every word, including duplicates.

Example:

bella  → l = 2
label  → l = 2
roller → l = 2

So answer has:  l, l

For every character, we keep the minimum frequency across all words.
Common frequency = minimum frequency among all words.

Logic:
Put character frequencies of the first word into map.
For every other word:
  Create curr frequency map.
  For every character in map:
    If it exists in curr, keep the minimum frequency.
    Otherwise, frequency becomes 0.
Add each character to ans according to its final frequency.
if(curr.containsKey(ch)){
    map.put(ch, Math.min(map.get(ch), curr.get(ch)));
}
else{
    map.put(ch, 0);
}
Why min?
bella  → l = 2
label  → l = 2
roller → l = 1

We can only use 1 l, because "roller" has only 1.

min(2,2,1) = 1


Code:
class Solution {
    public List<String> commonChars(String[] words) {
        HashMap<Character,Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
        // Put the first word
        for(char ch: words[0].toCharArray()){
            map.put(ch,map.getOrDefault(ch,0)+1);
        }

        // Put all the other words inside another hashmap
        for(int i=1;i<words.length;i++){
            HashMap<Character, Integer> curr = new HashMap<>();

            for(char ch: words[i].toCharArray()){
                curr.put(ch,curr.getOrDefault(ch,0)+1);
            }

            // For each word in main map, check if it exists in the curr map, if so put the minimum frequency. 
            // For a character to be common, the answer can contain only as many copies as the word with the fewest copies.
            
            for(char ch: map.keySet()){
                if(curr.containsKey(ch)){
                    map.put(ch,Math.min(map.get(ch),curr.get(ch)));
                }
                else{
                    map.put(ch,0);
                }
            }
        }

        List<String> ans = new ArrayList<>();
        for(Map.Entry<Character,Integer> entry: map.entrySet()){
            char ch = entry.getKey();
            int freq= entry.getValue();

            while(freq>0){
                ans.add(String.valueOf(ch));
                freq--;
            }
        }

        return ans;
    }
}
